# The back end's settings for your own computer. To use them, copy this file to `.env` in this
# folder (in PowerShell, from the repo root: Copy-Item backend\.env.example backend\.env), then
# fill in your own values there. Git ignores `.env`, so your key never leaves your computer.
# Never put a real key in this file: it is in the repo for everyone to read.

# The key for Anthropic's API, made at console.anthropic.com. Empty means no AI: the fixed
# challenge question is asked every time and
# the word rule judges every hazard.
TAKE5_AI_KEY=

# Which company's AI writes the challenge question. Only claude for now.
# TAKE5_AI_PROVIDER=claude

# Which of its models writes the challenge question. Left out, it is claude-opus-5-5.
# TAKE5_AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5

# Which of its models judges whether a hazard is vague. Left out, it is claude-haiku-5-5.
# TAKE5_AI_HAZARD_MODEL=claude-haiku-5-5

# Where saved Take 5s are kept. Left out, it is backend/.data/take5.sqlite3.
# TAKE5_DATABASE_PATH=C:\dev\take5-test.sqlite3
